From d156d87d9f868a48eaa31b7988f814b366f737e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:58:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A shape flashed on the ground as an ability lands:
 PlayGroundBurst

PlayGroundBurst(x, y, z, facing, shape, reach, arc, seconds, colour[, width]) lays an ability's
shape at that spot as a burst: a shock front in the colour runs from the spot out to the edge
over most of the time and fades after, with a flash of the whole shape under it that goes out
first. The shapes are the telegraphs' (a wedge, a ring, a strip) on the world decal, the
textures made here. An effect, like a weapon trail, not a floor marker: drawn whatever the
markers are set to, for the caster too (Shockwave's cone, where the spell look is a ring).
HasActionCombat() is 18.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
